# Tekne's kernel comes from excalibur-backports (DEC-036): newer laptop
# hardware needs it (e.g. ASUS ROG keyboards on hid-asus). Only the kernel
# packages are pinned up; everything else keeps the suite's default priority
# (NotAutomatic), so it can't replace a stable package unless asked for.
# linux-base is the kernel's install-helper package: 7.2 pre-depends on a newer
# one than stable's.
Package: linux-base linux-image-amd64 linux-image-*-amd64 linux-headers-amd64 linux-headers-*-amd64 linux-base-amd64 linux-base-*-amd64 linux-binary-*-amd64 linux-modules-*-amd64 linux-kbuild-* linux-compiler-*
Pin: release n=excalibur-backports
Pin-Priority: 500
